WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.555
Most job posts name Snowflake or Databricks.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:05.455
Interviewers go past the brochure.

3
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:08.115
They ask how it works, and what it costs.

4
00:00:08.135 --> 00:00:10.465
So learn each platform in one picture.

5
00:00:10.485 --> 00:00:12.815
Then learn how to choose.

6
00:00:12.835 --> 00:00:15.375
First: Snowflake has three layers.

7
00:00:15.395 --> 00:00:16.837
Storage holds the data.

8
00:00:16.857 --> 00:00:19.038
Virtual warehouses run the queries.

9
00:00:19.058 --> 00:00:21.960
A services layer plans and secures.

10
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.873
Storage and compute are separate.

11
00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:26.520
So each team can have its own warehouse.

12
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.833
Data sits in small blocks called micro-partitions.

13
00:00:29.853 --> 00:00:32.630
Each one knows its minimum and maximum.

14
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.380
A good filter lets Snowflake skip most blocks.

15
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.355
That is pruning.

16
00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:40.465
Second: three Snowflake features they ask about.

17
00:00:40.485 --> 00:00:44.825
Time travel reads a table as it was, some hours or days ago.

18
00:00:44.845 --> 00:00:47.100
A clone copies a table in seconds.

19
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.660
It shares the same blocks, so it costs nothing at first.

20
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.085
And Snowpipe loads new files as they land, with no schedule.

21
00:00:55.105 --> 00:00:57.520
Third: Databricks is a lakehouse.

22
00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.505
Your data stays as Delta tables, in your own cloud storage.

23
00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:05.340
Spark clusters and SQL warehouses run on top of it.

24
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.065
And Unity Catalog governs it all: names, grants, and lineage, in one place.

25
00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:13.050
Last: which one do you pick?

26
00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.850
Mostly SQL and analysts?

27
00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:17.135
Snowflake is simple to run.

28
00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:19.448
Heavy Spark, streaming, or machine learning?

29
00:01:19.468 --> 00:01:21.370
Databricks fits better.

30
00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.670
In the interview, give one recommendation.

31
00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.970
Then say its trade-off.

32
00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.405
Quick recap of the two platforms.

33
00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:30.818
Snowflake separates storage and compute.

34
00:01:30.838 --> 00:01:32.930
Databricks is Delta plus Spark.

35
00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.990
And always name the trade-off.

36
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.110
Now start the first lesson below.
